410:<div class="page-wrapper">
474:            <div class="mechanic-label" style="color: var(--gold-light);">Faction Bonus — Club</div>
475:            <p style="font-size:14px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:14px;">Fielding multiple Club faction heroes grants the <em>entire team</em> bonus ATK and HP. Thresholds:</p>
477:              <li><strong style="color:var(--gold-light);">3 Club heroes:</strong> +15% ATK &amp; HP for the team</li>
478:              <li><strong style="color:var(--gold-light);">3 + 2 (mixed):</strong> +25% ATK &amp; HP for the team</li>
479:              <li><strong style="color:var(--gold-light);">4 Club heroes:</strong> +30% ATK &amp; HP for the team</li>
480:              <li><strong style="color:var(--gold-light);">5 Club heroes:</strong> +35% ATK &amp; HP for the team — maximum bonus</li>
482:            <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-top:14px; font-style:italic;">Based on skill mechanics, Nuba could benefit from sustained HP (enabling her revive to matter more) and amplified ATK (making her Stun windows hit harder). Maximizing the Club faction count could strengthen her kit.</p>
759:            <p style="font-size:14px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:14px; line-height:1.5;">Mengpo originates from Chinese mythology as the keeper of the Bridge to the Afterlife. Every soul crossing receives her soup that erases memory of the life just lived - a mercy enabling rebirth without the burden of the past. The game draws directly on this mythology for her mechanics.</p>
1113:            <p style="font-size:14px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:14px; line-height:1.5;">Skadi originates from Norse mythology as the goddess of winter, mountains, and hunting. A Jotunn (giant) by birth, she married into the Aesir after the death of her father Thjazi. Known for her fierce independence and mastery of ice and snow, she chose to live in the frozen mountains rather than the warm halls of the gods. The game draws directly on this mythology for her mechanics.</p>
1470:            <p style="font-size:14px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:14px; line-height:1.5;">In Chinese mythology, the Plague God (Wen-Shen, or the Pestilence Deity) is not a figure of malice but of sacrifice. According to legend: "When humanity had no cure, Wen-Shen willingly drew all diseases upon herself in exchange for the health of the mortal world." She is a deity who chose suffering as an act of compassion.</p>
1499:            <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted); line-height:1.7; font-family: monospace;">
1850:            <p style="font-size:14px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:14px; line-height:1.5;">Hera is the queen of the Olympian gods in Greek mythology - goddess of marriage, family, and sovereign power. Wife and sister of Zeus, she is famous for her fierce jealousy, her dominion over the fates of heroes and enemies alike, and her absolute authority over those within her domain. The game draws directly on these themes for her mechanical identity.</p>
1876:            <div class="mechanic-label" style="color: var(--gold-light);">Internal Kit Synergy</div>
2217:            <p style="font-size:14px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:14px; line-height:1.5;">Jiutian Xuannv (九天玄女) is a celestial goddess from Chinese mythology - a divine strategist who advised the Yellow Emperor in his wars against Chi You. She embodies cosmic order, military wisdom, and the principle that a superior strategist reads the entire battlefield before making a single move. The game draws directly on these themes for her mechanical identity.</p>
2243:            <div class="mechanic-label" style="color: var(--gold-light);">Why Positioning Is Non-Negotiable</div>
2583:            <p style="margin-bottom:12px; color:var(--text-muted); font-size:14px; line-height:1.6;">Three devices appear on the field the moment the fight starts. They do nothing yet. Each time Hephaestus uses his Ultimate, he switches one on. A switched-on device creates a zone - allies inside it slowly recover HP and energy, enemies inside it become slower and weaker.</p>
2584:            <p style="margin-bottom:12px; color:var(--text-muted); font-size:14px; line-height:1.6;">After the second device is on, his laser and his shield become noticeably stronger. The laser holds enemies in place for longer, the shield reduces more damage.</p>
2585:            <p style="color:var(--text-muted); font-size:14px; line-height:1.6;">When all three are running, they merge. For five seconds, your entire team deals 30% more damage and attacks 50% faster, while the entire enemy team deals less. That is the moment you want your carry to fire. Every Ultimate he casts after that triggers the same five-second window again.</p>
2838:            <p style="font-size:14px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:14px; line-height:1.5;">Cronus draws on the Greek mythological figure associated with time - frequently conflated with Kronos the Titan and Khronos the personification of time in later traditions. In the game, Cronus is titled God of Time and is officially described as a Starglint faction Support whose identity revolves around rewinding allies, reducing cooldowns , and summoning projections . The game channels this mythological duality into his mechanical design as a master of temporal flow on the battlefield.</p>
2855:              <li>Cronus's Relic (<strong>Doctrine of Time</strong>) grants the skill <strong>Ferry of Time</strong>: every <strong>15 seconds</strong>, Cronus projects a Translucent Echo of an allied god into battle for <strong>6 seconds</strong>. <span style="font-size:11px; color:var(--text-muted); font-style:italic;">[Verified - EN Client]</span></li>
2865:            <div class="mechanic-label" style="color: var(--gold-light);">Why Relic Investment Matters - Competitive Breakpoints</div>
2888:              <span style="font-size:11px; color:var(--text-muted); font-style:italic; display:block; margin-top:4px;">[Verified - EN Client]</span>
2908:              <span style="font-size:11px; color:var(--text-muted); font-style:italic; display:block; margin-top:4px;">[Verified - EN Client]</span>
2928:              <span style="font-size:11px; color:var(--text-muted); font-style:italic; display:block; margin-top:4px;">[Verified - EN Client]</span>
2948:              <span style="font-size:11px; color:var(--text-muted); font-style:italic; display:block; margin-top:4px;">[Verified - EN Client]</span>
2968:              <span style="font-size:11px; color:var(--text-muted); font-style:italic; display:block; margin-top:4px;">[Verified - EN Client]</span>
3040:          <p style="font-size:12px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:16px; font-style:italic;">These are best-fit compositions based on mechanical role analysis. They are plausible and well-reasoned but not yet verified as established CN-meta standard lineups.</p>
3098:          <p style="font-size:12px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:16px; font-style:italic;">The following partners are role-fit synergies based on mechanical analysis - not verified CN-meta top picks. They represent the strongest archetype matches derived from Cronus's skill text.</p>
3232:            <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted); line-height:1.7;">
3237:            <div class="mechanic-label" style="color: var(--gold-light);">Relic Breakpoints - Endless Echo</div>
3357:            <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted); line-height:1.7;">
3364:            <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted); line-height:1.7; margin-top:8px;">
3379:            <div class="mechanic-label" style="color: var(--gold-light);">Awakening Priority</div>
